# The monorepo root marks `*.ndjson -diff` because SESSION/TRANSCRIPT journals can carry
# non-UTF-8 bytes that break UTF-8 diff decoding. Census journals are the opposite case:
# validated, machine-written UTF-8 JSON whose whole design goal is DIFF-FRIENDLY append-only
# review (design §3) — a binary-flagged roster cannot be reviewed, and an unreviewable roster
# defeats the reason it is plaintext. A deeper .gitattributes overrides the parent for exactly
# this subtree, the same shape as this workspace's .gitignore re-including `packages/` against
# the parent's Swift-template `Packages/` rule.
census/*.ndjson diff
